 & =⟨-8,10,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{10}^{2}+(-11)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{285}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{285}}{2}.\n$$" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307169 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307170 13194139534745 true] [17592186307169 1089 "q-127908" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307169 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534745 true] [17592186307169 1100 "Calculate the area of the $△\\,PQR,$ if $P(2,6,6),$ $Q(4,8,2),$ $R(0,5,6).$" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307169 1113 #uuid "bfab2245-23fe-5c53-b308-d8d34e386f62" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307169 1145 "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(4i+8j+2k)-(2i+6j+6k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(5j+6k)-(2i+6j+6k) \\\\  & =-2i-j \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-4))i-(2\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot (-4))j+(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-4i+8j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-4,8,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{8}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{84} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{2}=\\sqrt{21}.\n$$" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307171 13194139534745 true] [17592186307170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307172 13194139534745 true] [17592186307170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307173 13194139534745 true] [17592186307170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307174 13194139534745 true] [17592186307170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307175 13194139534745 true] [17592186307170 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534745 true] [17592186307170 1041 "selection" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307170 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307172 13194139534745 true] [17592186307170 1110 #uuid "d72d58ea-9c27-534b-a1db-17d7b5f48986" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307171 1034 "\\frac{3\\sqrt{17}}{3}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307171 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307171 1111 #uuid "456be434-320b-533f-a895-738ed24c51ae" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307172 1034 "\\sqrt{21}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307172 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307172 1111 #uuid "dd00feb5-9a4c-55cb-b73f-45248954748a" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307173 1034 "2\\sqrt{21}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307173 1111 #uuid "2256c129-2c25-52b1-9888-e1dac674e987" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307174 1034 "\\sqrt{17}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307174 1111 #uuid "929d8742-8362-5df3-8fe1-96224a6cc0ad" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307175 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{2}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307175 1111 #uuid "2bc6ba1c-d0b6-5cfa-a5ea-1de5c0be7e5f" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307176 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307177 13194139534745 true] [17592186307176 1089 "q-128006" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307176 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534745 true] [17592186307176 1100 "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(4,-1,1),$ $B(0,-3,4),$ $C(2,1,4).$" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307176 1113 #uuid "baa1ec57-d442-586e-ad16-7b7f53918a50" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307176 1145 "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-3j+4k)-(4i-j+k) \\\\  & =-4i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+4k)-(4i-j+k) \\\\  & =-2i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 3)i-((-4)\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 3)j+((-4)\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-12i+6j-12k \\\\  & =⟨-12,6,-12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{324} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{18}{2}=9.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 9 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot \\sqrt{29} \\\\ 18 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{29} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{29}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{18\\sqrt{29}}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307178 13194139534745 true] [17592186307177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307179 13194139534745 true] [17592186307177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307180 13194139534745 true] [17592186307177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307181 13194139534745 true] [17592186307177 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307182 13194139534745 true] [17592186307177 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534745 true] [17592186307177 1041 "selection" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307177 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307180 13194139534745 true] [17592186307177 1110 #uuid "6e3bd006-8f11-5476-993d-39d4fa989ef5" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307178 1034 "\\frac{9\\sqrt{10}}{5}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307178 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307178 1111 #uuid "8a4d450c-f4a8-5f04-ba45-abaee3631b4e" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307179 1034 "\\frac{9\\sqrt{29}}{29}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307179 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307179 1111 #uuid "bd3bb152-cf7a-59e7-a2e0-18871709a79f" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307180 1034 "\\frac{18\\sqrt{29}}{29}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307180 1111 #uuid "8cb42673-e7f5-59cd-a7e9-f2f103e33af1" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307181 1034 "\\frac{6\\sqrt{33}}{11}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307181 1111 #uuid "3fcaa9a1-3762-54d7-a851-ba5270ca871a" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307182 1034 "\\frac{18\\sqrt{10}}{5}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307182 1111 #uuid "3503e25d-867e-5068-95b4-e7be0668fdb8" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307183 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307184 13194139534745 true] [17592186