\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,TUV$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{2}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $TU$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TU & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =VL\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ VL & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ VL & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307210 13194139534745 true] [17592186307209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307211 13194139534745 true] [17592186307209 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534745 true] [17592186307209 1041 "field-1" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307209 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307210 13194139534745 true] [17592186307209 1110 #uuid "28caeb49-f626-584b-aecf-3deecd660070" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307210 1034 "\\sqrt{6}" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307210 1111 #uuid "191fcae2-d836-58ef-9d69-61b65efd3a47" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307211 1034 "6" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534745 true] [17592186307211 1111 #uuid "93aa79ec-e915-5f14-9f4c-312bdc534daf" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307212 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307213 13194139534745 true] [17592186307212 1089 "q-316514" 13194139534745 true] [17592186307212 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534745 true] [17592186307212 1100 "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,DEF$, if $D(-1,2,0)$, $E(2,0,1)$, $F(1,3,2).$\n\n${A}_